---
const stats = [
  { n: '1,000+', d: 'tasks executed across multiple real organizations since 2025; the current ledger alone holds ~600 with full records', c: '#89b4fa' },
  { n: '3,057', d: 'agent sessions recorded, each with its mode, its turn count and its cost (45,485 conversation turns in total)', c: '#cba6f7' },
  { n: '6-8', d: 'human touches for one raw signal to become 22 executable briefs and 22 GitHub issues, on the measured reference run', c: '#d4af37' },
  { n: '~$2', d: 'agent spend for a full M-sized task, measured end to end from the ledger', c: '#a6e3a1' },
];
---

<section id="evidence" class="py-8 md:py-14 px-6 relative scroll-mt-14">
  <div class="continuum-rule max-w-7xl mx-auto absolute top-0 left-1/2 -translate-x-1/2 w-full"></div>
  <div class="max-w-7xl mx-auto">
    <span class="eyebrow mb-4 block" style="color: #d4af37;">Evidence</span>
    <h2 class="text-[1.875rem] md:text-[2.5rem] max-w-[620px] mb-4">
      Measured, not projected.
    </h2>
    <p class="text-text-muted max-w-[620px] mb-12">
      Continuum was built by its first user and has run his working life since 2025:
      his own products, client work inside a real enterprise engagement, and the studio
      behind it (Tiphareth Studio). The numbers below come out of the system's own
      ledger, because recording them is one of the things it does.
    </p>

    <div class="grid sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-4 gap-4 mb-10">
      {stats.map((s) => (
        <div class="glass-card p-6">
          <div class="font-mono text-[2rem] font-semibold text-text-primary" style={`color:${s.c}`}>{s.n}</div>
          <p class="text-[0.78125rem] text-text-muted mt-2 leading-relaxed">{s.d}</p>
        </div>
      ))}
    </div>

    <div class="glass-pane p-6 md:p-8 grid md:grid-cols-[1fr_auto] gap-6 items-center">
      <div>
        <h3 class="text-[1.0625rem] mb-2">The reference run</h3>
        <p class="text-[0.875rem] text-text-muted max-w-[640px]">
          One captured signal went in. Out came 17 findings, 9 decisions, 22 executable
          briefs and 22 GitHub issues, with the human touching the run 6 to 8 times,
          every touch a decision that was genuinely theirs to make. A signal is usually
          a few lines; the refinery does the expanding.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-3 text-[0.8125rem] italic text-text-secondary border-l-2 border-[rgba(212,175,55,0.5)] pl-4 max-w-[640px]">
          "This abstraction let me abstract from every detail and participate only where
          I was actually needed."
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="font-mono text-[0.6875rem] text-text-dim leading-loose whitespace-nowrap">
        <div>signal <span class="text-surface1">──</span> <span class="text-[#89dceb]">17 findings</span></div>
        <div>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; <span class="text-surface1">──</span> <span class="text-[#89b4fa]">9 decisions</span></div>
        <div>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; <span class="text-surface1">──</span> <span class="text-[#cba6f7]">22 briefs</span></div>
        <div>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; <span class="text-surface1">──</span> <span class="text-[#a6e3a1]">22 issues</span></div>
        <div>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; <span class="text-surface1">──</span> <span class="text-[#d4af37]">6-8 touches</span></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
